aven't used any yet. We need to decide our vote. We can either support D, or shift to another candidate based on evidence. Let's evaluate.\n\nCandidate A: strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: sometimes not good at taking criticism, regarded as a show-off. No info on stress resilience, crew cooperation, communication, adaptability, attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate B: strengths: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: can be grumpy, relatively weak memory for numbers. No info on crew cooperation, communication, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: makes correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in a crisis, 100% reliable. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education. No explicit technical competence, attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, know-it-all, weak leadership, moody.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention/accuracy, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's compare.\n\nReliability: C is 100% reliable. D also seems reliable (takes responsibility, problem solving). A unknown. B very conscientious (reliability). So multiple.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress very well. C keeps calm in crisis. D responds to unexpected events adequately (some). A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision (maybe technical). B excellent computer skills, good at assessing weather (technical). C makes correct decisions quickly (cognitive). D solves problems extremely well, concentrates well (technical). All have some.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly. D solves problems extremely well. A anticipates dangerous situations (decision). B unknown.\n\nAttention/accuracy: D concentrates very well. B weak memory for numbers (concern). A unknown. C unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: A regarded as show-off, not good at criticism (maybe poor). B can be grumpy (maybe poor). C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric (poor). D regarded as arrogant, know-it-all, moody (poor). All have concerns.\n\nProfessional communication: A not good at criticism, show-off. B grumpy. C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. D arrogant, know-it-all. All have issues.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A very good leadership qualities (maybe responsibility). B very conscientious. C 100% reliable (responsibility). So many.\n\nAdaptability: Not much info. A not open to new ideas. B unknown. C not willing to further education (low adaptability). D unknown.\n\nThus all have concerns. Which candidate has the best overall? Possibly Candidate B: strong stress handling, conscientious, good weather assessment, computer skills, but has grumpy and weak memory for numbers (attention). Crew cooperation unknown. Candidate C: reliability, calm, correct decisions, but communication issues and egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Candidate D: strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but leadership weak, moody, arrogant. Candidate A: anticipates danger, leadership, but show-off, poor criticism.\n\nWe need to decide a vote. Considering the panel's need for crew cooperation and communication, all have issues. Which is least severe? Perhaps Candidate B's grumpiness and weak memory for numbers could be mitigated with training; stress handling is crucial for long-distance. Candidate C's egocentric and communication difficulty could be more severe for crew. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership could be severe. Candidate A's show-off and criticism issues also severe.\n\nThus I might lean toward Candidate B as the best overall, given strong stress resilience and conscientiousness, and technical skills, with concerns that may be less safety-critical than communication deficits.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's concerns about D and bring in evidence for B. Use explicit facts: B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concern: can be grumpy, weak memory for numbers. Argue that stress resilience is critical, and B's strengths outweigh concerns, and that D's crew cooperation concerns are more severe.\n\nThus we state our recommendation: Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: Agent 1 raised concerns about D's crew interaction; we agree that lack of evidence is problematic, and propose B as alternative.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
